{"height": 4, "weight": 58, "base_experience": 221, "ev_yield": [{"stat": "special-defense", "value": 3}], "genus": "Flower Pokémon", "capture_rate": 45, "base_happiness": 70, "hatch_counter": 20, "growth_rate": "medium-slow", "egg_groups": ["plant"], "gender_rate": 4, "names": [{"language": "ja-hrkt", "name": "キレイハナ"}, {"language": "ja-roma", "name": "Kireihana"}, {"language": "ko", "name": "아르코"}, {"language": "zh-hant", "name": "美麗花"}, {"language": "fr", "name": "Joliflor"}, {"language": "de", "name": "Blubella"}, {"language": "es", "name": "Bellossom"}, {"language": "it", "name": "Bellossom"}, {"language": "ja", "name": "キレイハナ"}, {"language": "zh-hans", "name": "美丽花"}, {"language": "es-419", "name": "Bellossom"}], "pokedex_entries": [{"versions": ["gold", "leafgreen"], "text": "BELLOSSOM gather at times and appear to dance. They say that the dance is a ritual to summon the sun."}, {"versions": ["silver", "firered", "soulsilver", "sword"], "text": "Plentiful in the tropics. When it dances, its petals rub together and make a pleasant ringing sound."}, {"versions": ["crystal"], "text": "When these dance together, their petals rub against each other, making pretty, relaxing sounds."}, {"versions": ["ruby"], "text": "When BELLOSSOM gets exposed to plenty of sunlight, the leaves ringing its body begin to spin around. This POKéMON’s dancing is renowned in the southern lands."}, {"versions": ["sapphire"], "text": "A BELLOSSOM grows flowers more beautifully if it has evolved from a smelly GLOOM - the stinkier the better. At night, this POKéMON closes its petals and goes to sleep."}, {"versions": ["emerald"], "text": "Its flower petals deepen in color through exposure to sunlight. When cloudy weather persists, it does a dance that is thought to be a ritual for summoning the sun."}, {"versions": ["diamond", "pearl", "platinum", "black", "white", "black-2", "white-2", "y"], "text": "When the heavy rainfall season ends, it is drawn out by warm sunlight to dance in the open."